    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Integrated assessment modeling",
    "problem": "Current climate impact assessments, using damage functions or multi-model comparisons with standardized scenarios, suffer from inconsistencies, inflexibility to new policies, and a failure to capture crucial cross-sectoral interactions and feedbacks.",
    "method": "To assess multi-sectoral climate impacts, the paper proposes integrating geospatially resolved, physical impact models into a self-consistent, coupled human-Earth system modeling framework as an alternative to using aggregated damage functions or rigid, standardized multi-model comparison exercises.",
    "task": "The task is to propose and demonstrate a consistent, integrated modeling framework, coupling a human-Earth system model with geospatially resolved impact models, to assess multi-sectoral climate impacts under new, responsive economic and policy scenarios.",
